 "id": "T11",
 "title": "Diabetes outreach registry: reverse chaining, chaining and includes",
 "scenario": "An outreach tool finds patients with poorly controlled diabetes (HbA1c > 9%) and pulls the supporting results and their provenance in one search. The server holds five patients, their lab Observations (one Observation references a patient that is not on this server), and Provenance records. All data is synthetic. You are checking what each search returns.",
 "server_timezone": "America/New_York",
 "why_hard": "Each _has parameter is evaluated independently (FHIR R4 search 3.1.1.4.16), so two _has conditions can be satisfied by two DIFFERENT Observations; binding code and value requires the code-value-quantity composite. Chained parameters are also independent. _include adds referenced resources that exist on the server (a dangling reference is silently omitted) and each appears once; _revinclude adds resources that point at a match, but not ones that point only at non-matches; included resources are not filtered by the search criteria.",
